# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Order matters — first match wins.
#
# 301s: the five /blog/footprint-finder-vs-* articles were consolidated into
# the /vs/:competitor pages they were cannibalising. Permanent redirects pass
# the accumulated ranking signals to the surviving URL; anything softer
# (302, client-side only, canonical-only) leaves them stranded.
#
# The `!` forces the rule even though a prerendered file may still exist at
# the old path in a stale deploy.
/blog/footprint-finder-vs-incogni    /vs/incogni     301!
/blog/footprint-finder-vs-deleteme   /vs/deleteme    301!
/blog/footprint-finder-vs-optery     /vs/optery      301!
/blog/footprint-finder-vs-mine       /vs/mine        301!
/blog/footprint-finder-vs-aura       /vs/aura        301!
/blog/*                              /vs             301!
/blog                                /vs             301!

# SPA fallback for Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
# A real file at the requested path (e.g. the prerendered
# /guides/foo/index.html) is always served first; this rule only handles
# routes with no matching static file (auth, dashboard, etc.).
/*    /index.html   200
